{t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t)}=\\frac{{s}^{2}-{\\omega }^{2}}{({s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2})^{2}},$ find the Laplace transform $L{{e}^{4t}\\cdot t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)}.$" 13194139535979 true] [17592186377989 1113 #uuid "e9ec4f95-ebe0-557a-aaf9-41fafa0a7395" 13194139535979 true] [17592186377989 1145 "The first shifting theorem states that if\n$L{f(t)}=F(s),$\nthen\n$L{{e}^{at}f(t)}=F(s-a).$\n\nUsing the given result, we have\n\n$$\nL{t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)}=\\frac{{s}^{2}-{3}^{2}}{({s}^{2}+{3}^{2})^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the first shifting theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{4t}\\cdot t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)} & =\\frac{(s-4)^{2}-{3}^{2}}{((s-4)^{2}+{3}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(s-4)^{2}-9}{((s-4)^{2}+9)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535979 true] [17592186377990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377991 13194139535979 true] [17592186377990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377992 13194139535979 true] [17592186377990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377993 13194139535979 true] [17592186377990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377994 13194139535979 true] [17592186377990 1000 #edb/ref 17592186377995 13194139535979 true] [17592186377990 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535979 true] [17592186377990 1041 "selection" 13194139535979 true] [17592186377990 1104 #edb/ref 17592186377991 13194139535979 true] [17592186377990 1110 #uuid "088e17fb-065d-5075-be80-c3df5393a43c" 13194139535979 true] [17592186377991 1034 "\\frac{(s-4)^{2}-9}{((s-4)^{2}+9)^{2}}" 13194139535979 true] [17592186377991 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535979 true] [17592186377991 1111 #uuid "6d7a3734-1dc5-5ee5-8061-9ff27cec1438" 13194139535979 true] [17592186377992 1034 "\\frac{(s-4)^{2}-9}{(s-4)^{2}+9}" 13194139535979 true] [17592186377992 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535979 true] [17592186377992 1111 #uuid "55142dcb-7399-596a-8681-57aad06734f9" 13194139535979 true] [17592186377993 1034 "\\frac{{s}^{2}-9}{((s-4)^{2}+9)^{2}}" 13194139535979 true] [17592186377993 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535979 true