6378016 1111 #uuid "9f13336f-d5b1-55e2-8a72-5c665c4d8bfc" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378017 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378018 13194139535979 true] [17592186378017 1089 "q-332133" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378017 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535979 true] [17592186378017 1100 "Given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{n}} & =\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}, &  & s>0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nuse linearity of Laplace transforms and the first shifting theorem to find the Laplace transform of $f(t)=5{t}^{2}+9t{e}^{3t}$ for $s>3.$" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378017 1113 #uuid "349d4b15-ca25-58c6-9fd5-8cd3227b330d" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378017 1145 "First, we apply the linearity properties of Laplace transforms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =L{5{t}^{2}+9t{e}^{3t}} \\\\  & =L{5{t}^{2}}+L{9t{e}^{3t}} \\\\  & =5L{{t}^{2}}+9L{t{e}^{3t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are given that, for $s>0,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{n}} & =\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{t} & =\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}} \\\\ L{{t}^{2}} & =\\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first shifting theorem states that if $L{f(t)}=F(s),$ then $L{{e}^{at}f(t)}=F(s-a).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nL{t{e}^{3t}}=\\frac{1}{(s-3)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =5L{{t}^{2}}+9L{t{e}^{3t}} \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{2}{{s}^{3}}+9\\cdot \\frac{1}{(s-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{9}{(s-3)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis transform is valid for $s>3.$" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378018 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378019 13194139535979 true] [17592186378018 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378020 13194139535979 true] [17592186378018 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378021 13194139535979 true] [17592186378018 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378022 13194139535979 true] [17592186378018 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378023 13194139535979 true] [17592186378018 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535979 true] [17592186378018 1041 "selection" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378018 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378021 13194139535979 true] [17592186378018 1110 #uuid "cf03c69d-8514-5c63-85ee-d03362b60eae" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378019 1034 "\\frac{10}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{9}{(s-3)^{3}}" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378019 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535979 true] [17592186378019 1111 #uuid "bfc05374-8f5e-526e-ac2e-dec8b6bac9d8" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378020 1034 "\\frac{10}{{s}^{2}}+\\frac{9}{(s-3)^{3}}" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378020 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535979 true] [17592186378020 1111 #uuid "e9cc487a-56e7-556f-b9e9-5cb13210c5a4" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378021 1034 "\\frac{10}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{9}{(s-3)^{2}}" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378021 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535979 true] [17592186378021 1111 #uuid "5a6a1a56-37ef-548b-92db-53d6dffdef0c" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378022 1034 "\\frac{10}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{3}{(s-3)^{2}}" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378022 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535979 true] [17592186378022 1111 #uuid "eaa2cebc-1ee2-5848-836e-c482688489a6" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378023 1034 "\\frac{5}{{s}^{3}}+\\frac{9}{(s-3)^{2}}" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378023 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535979 true] [17592186378023 1111 #uuid "476a0af2-cc7b-5b38-8b09-ccf3f76f2a3e" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378024 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378025 13194139535979 true] [17592186378024 1089 "q-332183" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378024 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535979 true] [17592186378024 1100 "Given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{n}} & =\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}, &  & s>0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nuse linearity of Laplace transforms and the first shifting theorem to find the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{4t}+5{t}^{3}{e}^{-t}$ for $s>4.$" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378024 1113 #uuid "b7eba2fe-279d-5114-9243-1203baad1a5e" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378024 1145 "First, we apply the linearity properties of Laplace transforms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =L{{e}^{4t}+5{t}^{3}{e}^{-t}} \\\\  & =L{{e}^{4t}}+L{5{t}^{3}{e}^{-t}} \\\\  & =L{{e}^{4t}}+5L{{t}^{3}{e}^{-t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are given that, for $s>0,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{n}} & =\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{3}} & =\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first shifting theorem states that if $L{f(t)}=F(s),$ then $L{{e}^{at}f(t)}=F(s-a).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{3}{e}^{-t}} & =\\frac{6}{(s+1)^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =L{{e}^{4t}}+5L{{t}^{3}{e}^{-t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-4}+5\\cdot \\frac{6}{(s+1)^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-4}+\\frac{30}{(s+1)^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis transform is valid for $s>4.$" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378025 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378026 13194139535979 true] [17592186378025 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378027 13194139535979 true] [17592186378025 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378028 13194139535979 true] [17592186378025 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378029 13194139535979 true] [17592186378025 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378030 13194139535979 true] [17592186378025 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535979 true] [17592186378025 1041 "selection" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378025 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378029 13194139535979 true] [17592186378025 1110 #uuid "d4bf1113-7bca-570e-9f5a-2b0d9d7450b7" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378026 1034 "\\frac{4}{s-4}+\\frac{30}{(s+1)^{4}}" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378026 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535979 true] [17592186378026 1111 #uuid "01207b56-c7b7-5d71-b917-f9c259b96270" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378027 1034 "\\frac{1}{s+4}+\\frac{30}{(s+1)^{4}}" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378027 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535979 true] [17592186378027 1111 #uuid "97f4ca32-717d-5b51-bf34-80479722f184" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378028 1034 "\\frac{1}{s-4}+\\frac{6}{(s+1