=5\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+1}+3\\cdot \\frac{6}{(s-2)^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{s+1}+\\frac{18}{(s-2)^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis transform is valid for $s>2.$" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378032 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378033 13194139535979 true] [17592186378032 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378034 13194139535979 true] [17592186378032 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378035 13194139535979 true] [17592186378032 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378036 13194139535979 true] [17592186378032 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378037 13194139535979 true] [17592186378032 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535979 true] [17592186378032 1041 "selection" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378032 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378037 13194139535979 true] [17592186378032 1110 #uuid "3fc1a32e-0c5e-5f80-8d30-a7fe77f30ec0" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378033 1034 "\\frac{5}{s+1}+\\frac{18}{(s+2)^{4}}" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378033 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535979 true] [17592186378033 1111 #uuid "728d1bd0-854f-5db8-972a-b2dcf7cb20fd" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378034 1034 "\\frac{5}{s-1}+\\frac{18}{(s+2)^{4}}" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378034 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535979 true] [17592186378034 1111 #uuid "22da784f-5fbf-5dfd-8501-d123f391ab58" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378035 1034 "\\frac{5}{s-1}+\\frac{18}{(s-2)^{4}}" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378035 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535979 true] [17592186378035 1111 #uuid "e50fba9a-42ec-5536-998b-8f7ba58a8073" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378036 1034 "\\frac{5}{s+1}+\\frac{6}{(s-2)^{4}}" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378036 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535979 true] [17592186378036 1111 #uuid "d5a2ead2-0349-5752-bc22-147593e0d8fa" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378037 1034 "\\frac{5}{s+1}+\\frac{18}{(s-2)^{4}}" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378037 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535979 true] [17592186378037 1111 #uuid "21adcb68-5bfc-5ff6-8479-1f92eebd73d9" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378038 1017 #edb/ref 17592186378039 13194139535979 true] [17592186378038 1089 "q-332199" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378038 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535979 true] [17592186378038 1100 "Given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{n}} & =\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}, &  & s>0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nuse linearity of Laplace transforms and the first shifting theorem to find the Laplace transform of  $f(t)=6{e}^{2t}+2{t}^{3}{e}^{-4t}$ for $s>2.$" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378038 1113 #uuid "025143ae-62a8-5506-b379-b3b2619c5b55" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378038 1145 "First, we apply the linearity properties of Laplace transforms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =L{6{e}^{2t}+2{t}^{3}{e}^{-4t}} \\\\  & =L{6{e}^{2t}}+L{2{t}^{3}{e}^{-4t}} \\\\  & =6L{{e}^{2t}}+2L{{t}^{3}{e}^{-4t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are given that, for $s>0,$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{n}} & =\\frac{n!}{{s}^{n+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{3}} & =\\frac{6}{{s}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first shifting theorem states that if $L{f(t)}=F(s),$ then $L{{e}^{at}f(t)}=F(s-a).$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{3}{e}^{-4t}} & =\\frac{6}{(s+4)^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =6L{{e}^{2t}}+2L{{t}^{3}{e}^{-4t}} \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-2}+2\\cdot \\frac{6}{(s+4)^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{s-2}+\\frac{12}{(s+4)^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis transform is valid for $s>2.$" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378039 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378040 13194139535979 true] [17592186378039 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378041 13194139535979 true] [17592186378039 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378042 13194139535979 true] [17592186378039 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378043 13194139535979 true] [17592186378039 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378044 13194139535979 true] [17592186378039 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535979 true] [17592186378039 1041 "selection" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378039 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378044 13194139535979 true] 