)}=F(s),$\nthen\n$L{{e}^{at}f(t)}=F(s-a).$\n\nThis implies that multiplying a function $f(t)$ by ${e}^{at}$ shifts the corresponding Laplace transform horizontally along the $s$-axis.\n\n- If $a>0,$ the graph of $F(s)$ shifts to the right.\n\n- If $a<0,$ the graph of $F(s)$ shifts to the left.\n\nIn our case, to get the graph of $L{{e}^{-6t}f(t)},$ we must shift the graph of $F(s)$ by $6$ units to the left.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/assets/fe5d17ffdb189defcd001b26eadf333df4d19157af44beeaa4c270083d1a625d.png)" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378046 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378047 13194139535979 true] [17592186378046 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378048 13194139535979 true] [17592186378046 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378049 13194139535979 true] [17592186378046 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378050 13194139535979 true] [17592186378046 1000 #edb/ref 17592186378051 13194139535979 true] [17592186378046 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535979 true] [17592186378046 1041 "selection" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378046 1104 #edb/ref 17592186378051 13194139535979 true] [17592186378046 1110 #uuid "93e24b6f-17c2-5027-bd94-2dc045f1912e" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378047 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/assets/afbe8291979d90666756181ca898851c5f0f30755ba985c32d56bd4b65e1fa5d.png" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378047 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535979 true] [17592186378047 1111 #uuid "ddd00a10-d84c-5e26-91e0-07cdcb69f2bd" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378048 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072996/assets/15227beae514ccbfe85f3ba5d1ac4bd47fc130c5c15ff4ecd4de1a2813f8f2db.png" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378048 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139535979 true] [17592186378048 1111 #uuid "28fd8864-3dac-5d8d-b61b-90d3064cb949" 13194139535979 true] [17592186378049 103